c1-b271-583fe4966ec5" :question/math-academy-id "q-48040" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/59c02273515e87fcebb8eb1785dc2cf0c6490feda4fc9644df43b8849921eec5.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ exists\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-1$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is true. The function $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-1$ and we have $f(-1)=1.$\n\n- Statement II is false. We get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{-}}f(x) & =2, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{1}^{+}}f(x) & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, both left-hand side and right-hand side limits exist but they are not the same. Therefore, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-1}f(x)$ does not exist.\n\n- Statement III is false. The function contains a break exactly at $x=-1$ and it's impossible to draw its graph without taking our pencil off of the paper." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-48040/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-48040"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-48080"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/374abcb470bfde0688def89290c8c1d639bf025afde150ccb9dd848c1fcc9a0f.png)\n\nWhat are the points of discontinuity of the function plotted above?" :question/worked-solution "The graph breaks at $x=-2$ and $x=0$ meaning that we can't draw the plot without taking our pencil off of the paper when passing through these points.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x=-2$ and $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" :answer/id #uuid "b0860d22-ccb0-51ef-94f5-2a6c1dc93bff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" :answer/id #uuid "0d0f2583-9b59-5da9-b54d-1b663a571f98" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection/ab63e789ad10d34c2ff41e36a494d8b1a65dadbef60dc438a2edd1b43cabc88a" :answer/id #uuid "41802a34-2f4f-586f-959c-44a51f853fb5" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=2$ and $x=0$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" :answer/id #uuid "ce306621-d6f8-5102-86d6-206fc70fe17b" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer/id #uuid "91153512-cc48-5d37-bd38-b2e9e9a281d1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "06492b5e-292d-55de-94e3-eed67f0b3b2d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-48087/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee" :answer-field/choices ["q-48087/selection/7f44eea92af5c9acdec8919ce008f32aaa724d76d416ab5243173911577f9642" "q-48087/selection/1288db97e8c08fe1e59253bc39f36416fd21e4daf73730ee4bb5aebee1b12042" "q-48087/selection/ab63e789ad10d34c2ff41e36a494d8b1a65dadbef60dc438a2edd1b43cabc88a" "q-48087/selection/517b13fa7d7411493417798333c215e538be20515774e23158b4c71536604686" "q-48087/selection/0be40a41fff2075dcd7ae30d0e6284ddf7b2ec7e519882e4636a79e6edbe7cee"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-48087" :question/id #uuid "e1be977e-f400-57c2-8b54-c7545b58f2e9" :question/math-acad