e83dab8d50608e6db7ccaf97f5e1a8f2ee83d2f893e3d820c3.png)\n\nAll the other given graphs can be plotted without taking the pencil off of the paper." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104036/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "31eacf5a-75a5-5b38-8c24-4b1598ecf3a7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104036"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "d7ada344-5734-567e-8b91-6b033af9fcfa" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "0ccba1ce-df30-5537-9903-3539c59244a1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "d9318cab-6240-5247-92be-6dbae81f6d7c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "060f2bab-5815-509c-87b6-cca9bc209c9a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "4f4c715d-922e-5f15-a7c5-7d8861065287" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "32321e97-b95f-52de-bf4b-99684620297d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-104124/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer-field/choices ["q-104124/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" "q-104124/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-104124/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-104124/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-104124/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-104124" :question/id #uuid "af1da89e-6dd1-5d6d-99dd-762b173b6a23" :question/math-academy-id "q-104124" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13980753/assets/bdcfa35fb04028cbff32992b41214c878443d3815b676a0cf046f5a99bd771bd.png)\n\nThe graph of $y=f(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true? \n\n- $f(x)$ is **not** defined at $x=-2$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=f(-2)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-2$" :question/worked-solution "By inspecting the graph, we can conclude the following:\n\n- Statement I is false. Indeed, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=-2$ and $f(-2)=5.$\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, from the graph we see that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{-}}f(x) & =5, \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to \\,-{2}^{+}}f(x) & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{x\\to \\,-2}f(x)=5=f(-2).$\n\n- Statement III is true. The graph of $f(x)$ can be drawn without taking our pencil off of the paper in the neighborhood of $x=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-104124/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f92e521-e7ab-56ba-8eac-0484b140b1a2"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-104124"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
